PRODID:-//UNYD Process Guide//2027 Planning Calendar//EN
CALSCALE:GREGORIAN
METHOD:PUBLISH
X-WR-CALNAME:UNYD 2027 policy and negotiation planning
X-WR-CALDESC:Official session dates plus clearly labelled tentative preparation milestones. Historical precedents are not placed on the 2027 calendar.
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:csocd-2027-02-01-csocd65@unyd-process-guide
DTSTAMP:20260828T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270211
SUMMARY:CSocD: CSocD65
LOCATION:New York
DESCRIPTION:Official session dates.\nStatus: official. The sequence separates general priority-setting before the zero draft from clause-specific recommendations after it arrives. January timing uses the documented 2025 CSocD youth-resolution cycle as an early-warning pattern\, not a fixed CSocD rule.\nOfficial process source: https://social.desa.un.org/csocd/65th-session
URL:https://social.desa.un.org/csocd/65th-session
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:csw-2027-01-04-youth-recommendations@unyd-process-guide
DTSTAMP:20260828T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270104
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270118
SUMMARY:[Planning] CSW: Youth recommendations
LOCATION:New York
DESCRIPTION:Youth recommendations were developed for both CSW69 and CSW70\, but through different consultation arrangements. This projects a check-for-call window rather than an official 2027 deadline.\nStatus: tentative. Three routes are shown separately: the formal Agreed Conclusions route through the responsible ministry or the country’s Permanent Mission in New York\; repeated recent-cycle youth-recommendation and UN Women coordination\; and the annual CSW Youth Forum. Only the first route provides access to the intergovernmental draft.\nOfficial process source: https://www.unwomen.org/en/how-we-work/commission-on-the-status-of-women
URL:https://www.unwomen.org/en/how-we-work/commission-on-the-status-of-women
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:csw-2027-01-18-un-women-youth-office-briefing@unyd-process-guide
DTSTAMP:20260828T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270118
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270215
SUMMARY:[Planning] CSW: UN Women / Youth Office briefing
LOCATION:New York
DESCRIPTION:Briefings occurred in both recent cycles: a general CSW69 youth briefing on 14 February 2025 and a CSW70 pre-zero-draft meeting with national UN Youth Delegates on 20 January 2026. No fixed 2027 date or format is established.\nStatus: tentative. Three routes are shown separately: the formal Agreed Conclusions route through the responsible ministry or the country’s Permanent Mission in New York\; repeated recent-cycle youth-recommendation and UN Women coordination\; and the annual CSW Youth Forum. Only the first route provides access to the intergovernmental draft.\nOfficial process source: https://www.unwomen.org/en/how-we-work/commission-on-the-status-of-women
URL:https://www.unwomen.org/en/how-we-work/commission-on-the-status-of-women
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:csw-2027-03-07-csw-youth-forum-date-tbc@unyd-process-guide
DTSTAMP:20260828T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270307
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270315
SUMMARY:CSW: CSW Youth Forum · date TBC
LOCATION:New York
DESCRIPTION:The CSW Youth Forum is recurring and was held at CSW68\, CSW69 and CSW70. Its 2027 date and participation conditions have not yet been published.\nStatus: tentative. Three routes are shown separately: the formal Agreed Conclusions route through the responsible ministry or the country’s Permanent Mission in New York\; repeated recent-cycle youth-recommendation and UN Women coordination\; and the annual CSW Youth Forum. Only the first route provides access to the intergovernmental draft.\nOfficial process source: https://www.unwomen.org/en/how-we-work/commission-on-the-status-of-women
URL:https://www.unwomen.org/en/how-we-work/commission-on-the-status-of-women
END:VEVENT
